### NOTE: compilation to take far longer if manual/ltac proofs included

###############################################################################
### CCS (value-free, Milner 1989): textbook pairs and the Alternating Bit
### Protocol, and instances of CTrees' CCS laws. Fast (under 30s together),
### so built by default and in CI.
examples/CCS.v ### REQUIRED FOR BELOW
examples/Bisimilarity/CCS/PluginProofs.v ### Success
examples/Bisimilarity/CCS/LawProofs.v ### Success (CTrees' CCS laws, tau-laws; ~20s)
# examples/Bisimilarity/CCS/ABPProofs.v ### Success (ABP: abp <= spec; ~3.7 min, peaks ~4.2GB: run under a memory cap)
# examples/Bisimilarity/CCS/ABPBisimProofs.v ### Success (ABP: weak_bisimilar; ~3.8 min, peaks ~4.2GB: separate file, both in one process exceed 6GB)

###############################################################################
### Evaluation series: one lever each (width, semantic layers, nesting
### depth), sizes and Solve counts pinned with least bounds. Small instances,
### ~40s together, so built by default and in CI; scale them up for
### benchmarking.
examples/Evaluation/Base.v ### REQUIRED FOR BELOW
examples/Evaluation/Width.v ### Success (6, 18, 54 states; ~22s)
examples/Evaluation/Layers.v ### Success (6 states, 0-8 layers; ~2s)
examples/Evaluation/Depth.v ### Success (K = 1-8; ~16s)
### Scaled up, for benchmarking (bench/proofs.sh -s eval-large): too slow to
### build by default.
# examples/Evaluation/WidthLarge.v ### Success (n = 3, 162 states; ~7 min, ~3.9GB)
# examples/Evaluation/LayersLarge.v ### Success (16, 32, 64 layers; ~2 min, Qed dominates)
# examples/Evaluation/DepthLarge.v ### Success (K = 12, 16; ~10 min, ~3.1GB)

